{
  "title": "Coordinators C01b: Local Checkpointer seam over all 45 pipeline/scheduler state writes (state-only and patch-with-",
  "body": "Part of #902. Slice C01b routes every pipeline run-state write through one seam, a `Checkpointer`. The local implementation is the exact store call it replaces. #960 later supplies a shared implementation that turns these writes into durable checkpoints.\n\n## Problem\n`runs.state_json` and the run columns are written from 45 places in src/pipeline/ and src/scheduler.ts (as of the reviewed `main`). There are two operations with different semantics:\n- `store.setRunState(id, state)` writes state only and publishes nothing;\n- `store.updateRun(id, patch, state?)` writes columns and optionally state, publishes a `run` event, and returns the run.\n\nSome calls deliberately pass **no state**. The shutdown branch (engine.ts ~372) preserves the last durable checkpoint instead of in-memory state, and cancellation finalization (src/pipeline/cancellation.ts ~15) passes cleared state.\n\n## Invariants\n1. **Two operations, the same semantics as today:**\n   - `writeState(runId, state)` is exactly `store.setRunState`: no notification, no return value.\n   - `writeRun(runId, patch, state?)` is exactly `store.updateRun`. `state` stays optional, so `undefined` means \"keep the stored state\". It publishes the same `run` event and returns the same `Run`.\n2. **Every pipeline write goes through the seam.** That is every `setRunState` and `updateRun` call in src/pipeline/** and src/scheduler.ts, including:\n   - the shutdown and cancel branch (engine.ts ~372);\n   - `finalizeRecordedCancellation` (cancellation.ts ~15);\n   - scheduler startup (~41, ~57).\n\n   The PR lists each converted site, with its file and line.\n3. **Local behaviour is unchanged exactly:**\n   - the same store operation, arguments, return value and notifications, in the same order;\n   - no new await boundary. The local `checkpoint()` boundary is synchronous and returns `void`, and `save()` awaits only a returned promise. `RunContext.save()` still has no await after its write.\n4. **Writes outside the pipeline are listed, not converted.** Some writes come from elsewhere:\n   - src/integrations/github-notifier.ts (one `updateRun`);\n   - store-internal transactions (review-round creation, resolution, dependency failure);\n   - src/app.ts paths such as answer and cancel.\n\n   #960 and C19 (deferred) decide which of these become checkpoints.\n\n## Mechanism (src/pipeline/context.ts)\n```ts\nexport interface Checkpointer {\n  writeState(runId: string, state: RunState): void;\n  writeRun(runId: string, patch: RunPatch, state?: RunState): Run;\n  /** A durable boundary after a write. Local: synchronous, returns void. Shared (#960): may return a promise. */\n  checkpoint(runId: string, label?: string): void | Promise\u003cvoid\u003e;\n}\nexport function localCheckpointer(store: Store): Checkpointer;   // writeState→setRunState, writeRun→updateRun, checkpoint→no-op\n```\n- **Engine access.** `EngineDeps` gains `checkpointer?: Checkpointer`. A `RunContext` resolves `deps.checkpointer ?? localCheckpointer(deps.store)` once.\n- **`save(label)`** (~503): the fault hook, then `writeState`, then `const p = checkpoint(id, label); if (p) await p;`.\n- **Every site** in invariant 2 changes from `store.setRunState(...)` to `checkpointer.writeState(...)`, and from `store.updateRun(...)` to `checkpointer.writeRun(...)`, with identical arguments and positions.\n- **Scheduler and cancellation.** `Scheduler` and `finalizeRecordedCancellation` take the same checkpointer (a parameter defaulting to local), so the startup re-queue and the cancel finalization use it too.\n\n## Tests\n- Engine and scheduler tests with the existing fakes.\n- A recording `Checkpointer` wraps the local one and logs `(op, runId, patch keys, state present)`.\n- No network.\n\n1. **Traces of real paths.** With the recording checkpointer, run these through the real engine:\n   - prepare and one stage;\n   - a GitHub-wait re-queue;\n   - a needs-human ending;\n   - a post-merge rejection path;\n   - a **user cancel** (`finalizeRecordedCancellation`);\n   - a **daemon shutdown** during a stage (the engine.ts ~372 branch).\n\n   In each, every state and run write appears in the recording. A store spy sees no pipeline `setRunState` or `updateRun` call that didn't go through it. Removing the seam from the cancel or the shutdown branch fails this test.\n2. **Shutdown keeps the durable state.** On the shutdown branch, `writeRun` is called with `state` undefined, and the stored `state_json` afterwards equals the last checkpoint, not the in-memory state.\n3. **Notifications are unchanged:**\n   - A store subscriber counts `run` events across a full fake run; the count equals the same run without the seam.\n   - `writeState` publishes nothing.\n4. **Visibility and ordering:**\n   - Immediately after `save()`'s synchronous part (before any microtask turn), `store.getRunState(id)` returns the new state.\n   - **No added await, checked deterministically:** `const p = ctx.save(); let done = false; p.then(() =\u003e (done = true)); await null;` leaves `done === true` in local mode, as it does today. One added internal `await` makes it false.\n5. **Return values:** each converted `writeRun` returns the same `Run` that `updateRun` would, and the engine's `ctx.run` matches a run without the seam.\n6. **Local compatibility:** with no `checkpointer`, the existing engine, scheduler, cancellation and report tests pass unchanged, and the fault hook still fires before each save.\n\n## Compatibility\n- No migration, config or network call.\n- With the local checkpointer, behaviour is byte-identical.\n- An older release is unaffected.\n\n## Out of scope\n- The shared checkpointer (#960).\n- Converting writes outside src/pipeline/** and src/scheduler.ts.\n- Identities and schema (#948).\n\n## Budget\nAbout 95 source lines plus tests: the interface and local implementation about 25, `save()` about 5, 45 call sites about 50, and the scheduler and cancellation parameters about 15.\n\nStop and report past 135.\n"
}
</github-data-json>
